s three new stacks and frees 3 and 4, both of\nwhom needed only stack 0: one pairing where two are required.\n\n\\begin{theorem}[the repair is a matching condition]\\label{thm:matching}\nLet $Y=X\\setminus(S\\cup\\{q\\})$, and join each $d\\in Y$ to the stacks of\n$o(d,S)\\subseteq o(q,S)$. Then $q$ is hereditarily definite at $S$ iff this","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
